 Introduction to GitOps Tools

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m exploring popular GitOps tools that help automate deployments and manage infrastructure efficiently. 🚀
These tools enable teams to implement GitOps workflows in real-world DevOps environments.

🔹 Argo CD
 Argo CD is one of the most widely used GitOps tools for Kubernetes.
 It continuously monitors Git repositories and automatically synchronizes the Kubernetes cluster with the desired configuration stored in Git.
Key features include:
Automated deployments
Web UI for monitoring applications
Rollback using Git history

🔹 Flux CD
 Flux CD is another powerful GitOps tool designed to keep Kubernetes clusters synchronized with Git repositories.
It automatically detects changes in Git and applies them to the cluster, ensuring the system state always matches the repository configuration.

🔹 Jenkins X
 Jenkins X is a cloud-native CI/CD platform built specifically for Kubernetes.
 It integrates CI/CD pipelines with GitOps workflows to enable automated application delivery and environment management.

🔹 Fleet
 Fleet is a GitOps tool used for managing multiple Kubernetes clusters at scale.
 It allows organizations to deploy and manage applications across large fleets of clusters using Git repositories.

💡 Key Insight:
 GitOps tools act as automation engines that continuously monitor Git repositories and ensure the infrastructure or cluster matches the desired configuration.
